    "items": [
      {
        "id": "def-qft-qed-physical-gauge-quantities",
        "kind": "definition",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Charge, canonical photon field and observer units",
        "reference": "research/plan-quantum-field-theory-track.md#L592",
        "design_state": "Defines the SI and natural normalization dictionary for charge, potential, field strength and gauge functions.",
        "dependency_level": 3,
        "deps": [
          "def-qft-framework-units",
          "def-qft-qed-gauge-data",
          "def-countable-choice",
          "def-em-si-conventions",
          "def-em-electromagnetic-tensor",
          "def-em-gauge-transformation"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-qft-framework-units": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-qft-qed-gauge-data": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-em-si-conventions": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-em-electromagnetic-tensor": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-em-gauge-transformation": "formulation-prerequisite"
        },
        "physical_scope": "Charge and gauge-field conversions for the selected flat-space QED model, in the stated SI and natural normalizations; no charge value, running law, regulator, boundary charge sector, or interacting continuum construction is inferred.",
        "statement": "Use the oriented, time-oriented Minkowski model, length coordinates, metric,\nand SI/natural dictionary of [[def-qft-framework-units]], with\n$\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$ and $x^0=ct$. Use the gamma matrices,\nDirac adjoint, and effective Clifford metric of\n[[def-qft-qed-gauge-data]]: $\\gamma^0=\\beta$, $\\{\\gamma^a,\\gamma^b\\}=-2\\eta^{ab}I_4$,\nand $\\bar\\psi=\\psi^\\dagger\\beta$. Assume Countable Choice\n[[def-countable-choice]] for the mathematical QFT gauge-data supplier; the\nunit conversions below do not themselves spend a choice principle.\n\nIdentify the SI charge and mass symbols $q,m$ in\n[[def-qft-qed-gauge-data]] with $q_{\\rm SI},m_{\\rm SI}$ here. Its natural\ncoupling $g$ is $q_{\\rm n}$ below, and its inverse-length mass $\\mu$ is the\nsame $m_{\\rm SI}c/\\hbar$.\n\nLet $q_{\\rm SI}\\in\\mathbb R$ be a selected charge parameter in coulombs and\n$m_{\\rm SI}>0$ a selected rest-mass parameter in kilograms. They are inputs\nof the chosen model; neither is derived from Maxwell's equations. Set\n$\\mu=m_{\\rm SI}c/\\hbar$ in $\\mathrm m^{-1}$ and\n$q_{\\rm n}=q_{\\rm SI}\\sqrt{\\mu_0c/\\hbar}$, which is dimensionless under the\nframework units of [[def-qft-framework-units]]. For an electron use\n$q_{\\rm SI}=-e_{\\rm SI}$ and\n$e_{\\rm n}=e_{\\rm SI}\\sqrt{\\mu_0c/\\hbar}>0$, so $q_{\\rm n}=-e_{\\rm n}$.\nUse $\\varepsilon_0=(\\mu_0c^2)^{-1}$ with the measured current-SI\n$\\mu_0$ of [[def-qft-framework-units]]. These definitions therefore do not\nassign an exact numerical value to $q_{\\rm n}$, $e_{\\rm n}$, or\n$\\varepsilon_0$.\n\nIn a named inertial chart, let $A^\\mu_{\\rm SI}=(\\varphi/c,\\mathbf A)$ be the\nelectromagnetic potential when one is supplied, with components in\n$\\mathrm{T\\,m}$ under [[def-em-si-conventions]] and\n[[def-em-electromagnetic-tensor]]. Define the canonical potential and\nfield-strength components by\n\n$$a^\\mu:=\\frac{A^\\mu_{\\rm SI}}{\\sqrt{\\mu_0\\hbar c}},\\qquad f^{\\mu\\nu}:=\\frac{F^{\\mu\\nu}_{\\rm SI}}{\\sqrt{\\mu_0\\hbar c}}.$$\n\nThey have engineering dimensions $\\mathrm m^{-1}$ and $\\mathrm m^{-2}$,\nrespectively. With the metric-lowered potential\n$A_{{\\rm SI},a}=\\eta_{ab}A^b_{\\rm SI}$, the potential component convention is\n$A_{{\\rm SI},0}=-\\varphi/c$ and $A_{{\\rm SI},i}=A_i$. The covariant derivative\nin the selected QED model is\n\n$$D_a:=\\partial_a-iq_{\\rm n}a_a =\\partial_a-\\frac{iq_{\\rm SI}}{\\hbar}A_{{\\rm SI},a},$$\n\nsince $q_{\\rm n}a_a=q_{\\rm SI}A_{{\\rm SI},a}/\\hbar$. Both terms in $D_a$\nhave unit $\\mathrm m^{-1}$. If the SI gauge function $\\chi$ has unit\n$\\mathrm{Wb}=\\mathrm{T\\,m^2}$, then $q_{\\rm SI}\\chi/\\hbar$ is dimensionless;\nthe corresponding natural gauge function\n$\\lambda=\\chi/\\sqrt{\\mu_0\\hbar c}$ is dimensionless and\n$q_{\\rm n}\\lambda=q_{\\rm SI}\\chi/\\hbar$. These conversions apply to smooth\nlocal gauge transformations; they assert no boundary condition, asymptotic\ncharge sector, or global gauge-fixing result.\n\nIf a separately specified finite regulator introduces Hamiltonian\neigenvalues, they have unit joule; this definition introduces no regulator.\nThe field components and units refer to the selected inertial chart, not to a\nnew observer congruence or a cross-framework identification.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "not-applicable"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted full-text Chapter 6",
              "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S6.html",
              "locator": "§§6.1–6.3.1 for the Maxwell field, covariant potential, local Dirac coupling, and charge current; the source uses natural units and the opposite metric signature, translated explicitly here."
            },
            {
              "title": "Mark Srednicki, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted 2006 prepublication book draft",
              "url": "https://web.physics.ucsb.edu/~mark/ms-qft-DRAFT.pdf",
              "locator": "§12, printed pp. 104–105, for natural-unit dimensional bookkeeping; §§54 and 58, printed pp. 332–347, for Maxwell and spinor-electrodynamics conventions."
            }
          ]
        },
        "library": "physics"
      },
      {
        "id": "post-qft-free-photon-model",
        "kind": "postulate",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Positive transverse free photon model",
        "reference": "research/plan-quantum-field-theory-track.md#L592",
        "design_state": "Adopts the positive transverse free photon model conditionally on the actual QFT-MG01 carriers and current EM model conventions.",
        "dependency_level": 7,
        "deps": [
          "def-qft-framework-units",
          "def-qft-photon-transverse-space",
          "def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces",
          "post-qft-constructed-model-and-measurement",
          "lem-qft-photon-null-quotient",
          "lem-qft-photon-covariance-spectrum",
          "lem-qft-photon-local-weyl-observables",
          "post-em-vacuum-maxwell",
          "def-em-electromagnetic-tensor",
          "def-em-gauge-transformation",
          "def-countable-choice"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-qft-framework-units": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-qft-photon-transverse-space": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "post-qft-constructed-model-and-measurement": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "lem-qft-photon-null-quotient": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-photon-covariance-spectrum": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-photon-local-weyl-observables": "mathematical-premise",
          "post-em-vacuum-maxwell": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-em-electromagnetic-tensor": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-em-gauge-transformation": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "physical_scope": "The selected source-free, flat Minkowski Maxwell photon model with a positive transverse one-particle Hilbert space, its constructed bosonic Fock representation and free dynamics, and actual smeared field-strength and bounded Weyl observables; no interacting continuum QED or empirical outcome is asserted.",
        "statement": "Adopt the following specified free-photon model in the oriented,\ntime-oriented affine Minkowski spacetime and length coordinates of\n[[def-qft-framework-units]], with metric $(-,+,+,+)$ and $x^0=ct$. The\nclassical electromagnetic input is the smooth source-free branch of\n[[post-em-vacuum-maxwell]]; the electromagnetic two-form and its potential\ncomponents are those of [[def-em-electromagnetic-tensor]], and a supplied\npotential is subject to [[def-em-gauge-transformation]]. These EM suppliers\nare physical input and conventions: they do not by themselves construct a\nquantum representation.\n\nFor almost every $\\mathbf k\\in\\mathbb R^3\\setminus\\{0\\}$, set\n$\\mathbf n=\\mathbf k/|\\mathbf k|$ and\n$P_T(\\mathbf k)=I_3-\\mathbf n\\mathbf n^{\\mathsf T}$. The mathematical\ndefinition [[def-qft-photon-transverse-space]] specifies the positive\none-photon Hilbert space\n\n$$\\mathcal H_T= \\{u\\in L^2(\\mathbb R^3,d^3\\mathbf k;\\mathbb C^3): \\mathbf k\\cdot u(\\mathbf k)=0\\text{ for almost every }\\mathbf k\\},$$\n\nwith the inherited pairing\n$\\langle u,v\\rangle_2=\\int\\overline{u(\\mathbf k)}\\cdot v(\\mathbf k)\\,d^3\\mathbf k$,\nlinear in the second variable as in [[def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces]]. The\nvalue assigned to $P_T$ at\n$\\mathbf k=0$ is immaterial because that point has Lebesgue measure zero; no\ncontinuous polarization frame over all momentum directions is chosen. Adopt\nthe bosonic Fock representation $\\mathcal F_s(\\mathcal H_T)$ and the free\nHamiltonian\n\n$$H_\\gamma=\\hbar c\\,d\\Gamma(|\\mathbf k|),$$\n\nwhere on the $n$-photon sector $d\\Gamma(|\\mathbf k|)$ is multiplication by\n$\\sum_{r=1}^n|\\mathbf k_r|$ and is zero on the vacuum sector. Its exact\nself-adjoint domain and the unitary mass-cone action are those in the\nmathematical supplier [[lem-qft-photon-covariance-spectrum]]. The actual\nsmeared field-strength distributions and bounded Weyl operators are those\nconstructed in [[lem-qft-photon-local-weyl-observables]]; a pointwise\npotential or field-strength operator is not asserted to exist. These\nmathematical suppliers are draft carriers with mixed current Step 1 status: the\ntransverse-space, null-quotient, covariance-spectrum, framework-units, and\nC01 measurement carriers have current ready records; the local-Weyl carrier is\nescalated through its field-strength prerequisite. Readiness records are not\nindependent approval, and every use remains conditional on the exact statement\nand proof supplied.\n\nFor the physical interpretation of an actually constructed state and a\nsupplied normalized measurement instrument, use\n[[post-qft-constructed-model-and-measurement]]: Born probabilities are\nassigned only to that specified model and instrument. This postulate records\nthe model's free Maxwell quanta as photons. It does not assert that the\nmodel has been empirically confirmed, and it introduces no interacting\nfour-dimensional QED Hilbert space, scattering operator, LSZ limit,\nasymptotic completeness, or nonperturbative continuum limit. In calculations\nusing an indefinite four-polarization auxiliary space, only the positive\ntransverse model or its separately constructed null quotient is physical;\nfour auxiliary components are not four positive photon states.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "not-applicable"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted full-text Chapter 6",
              "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S6.html",
              "locator": "§6.1 for the source-free Maxwell field; §6.2, especially §6.2.1, for Coulomb-gauge transverse modes, the two physical polarizations, and the auxiliary Lorenz-gauge construction."
            },
            {
              "title": "Mark Srednicki, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted 2006 prepublication book draft",
              "url": "https://web.physics.ucsb.edu/~mark/ms-qft-DRAFT.pdf",
              "locator": "§§54–55, printed pp. 332–338, for the Maxwell potential, Coulomb-gauge transverse projector, free modes, two helicities, and Hamiltonian. The source uses Heaviside–Lorentz units and c=1; the adopted model retains the explicit SI conversion."
            }
          ]
        },
        "library": "physics"
      },
      {
        "id": "post-qft-qed-local-coupling",
        "kind": "postulate",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Explicit charged Dirac/Maxwell local coupling model",
        "reference": "research/plan-quantum-field-theory-track.md#L592",
        "design_state": "Adopts a smooth local classical Maxwell–Dirac coupling and its free-field correspondence; no interacting continuum QED construction is claimed.",
        "dependency_level": 8,
        "deps": [
          "def-qft-framework-units",
          "def-qft-qed-gauge-data",
          "post-qft-free-field-model",
          "def-qft-qed-physical-gauge-quantities",
          "post-qft-free-photon-model",
          "def-em-gauge-transformation",
          "def-countable-choice"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-qft-framework-units": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-qft-qed-gauge-data": "mathematical-premise",
          "post-qft-free-field-model": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-qft-qed-physical-gauge-quantities": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "post-qft-free-photon-model": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-em-gauge-transformation": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "physical_scope": "A smooth local classical Maxwell–Dirac coupling in the stated SI/natural conventions, with electron charge q=-e as the selected QED species and the separately adopted free photon and Dirac representations; it asserts no interacting continuum Hilbert space, global PDE solution, pointwise quantum current, scattering operator, or nonperturbative QED construction.",
        "statement": "Adopt a smooth local classical Maxwell–Dirac model on an open region of the\nflat spacetime specified by [[def-qft-framework-units]]. Let $A_{{\\rm SI},a}$\nbe a supplied real $C^\\infty$ electromagnetic covector potential and let\n$\\psi:\\!U\\to\\mathbb C^4$ be a $C^\\infty$ commuting spinor field. The charge\n$q_{\\rm SI}$ and rest mass $m_{\\rm SI}>0$ are model inputs; for the electron\ntake $q_{\\rm SI}=-e_{\\rm SI}$. Use the component, metric, Clifford, charge,\nfield-normalization, and unit conventions of\n[[def-qft-qed-gauge-data]], [[def-qft-qed-physical-gauge-quantities]],\n[[def-qft-framework-units]], and the electromagnetic suppliers of\n[[post-qft-free-photon-model]]. In particular,\n$D_a=\\partial_a-iq_{\\rm SI}A_{{\\rm SI},a}/\\hbar\n=\\partial_a-iq_{\\rm n}a_a$ and $\\mu=m_{\\rm SI}c/\\hbar$.\n\nAdopt the local action density in natural normalization\n\n$$\\mathcal L_{\\rm nat} =-\\frac14 f_{ab}f^{ab} +\\frac{i}{2}\\bigl(\\bar\\psi\\gamma^aD_a\\psi -(D_a\\bar\\psi)\\gamma^a\\psi\\bigr)-\\mu\\bar\\psi\\psi,$$\n\nwhere $f_{ab}=\\partial_a a_b-\\partial_ba_a$ on the region where the\npotential is supplied, $\\bar\\psi=\\psi^\\dagger\\beta$, and\n$D_a\\bar\\psi=\\partial_a\\bar\\psi+iq_{\\rm n}a_a\\bar\\psi$. The physical action\nis $S_{\\rm cl}=\\hbar\\int_U\\mathcal L_{\\rm nat}\\,d^4x$ with $x^0=ct$. For\ncompactly supported local variations this is the adopted classical\nMaxwell–Dirac formulation; its Euler–Lagrange consequences are not postulated\nas a proof in this item.\n\nFor a smooth gauge function $\\chi$ in webers, the adopted local\ntransformation is\n$A_{{\\rm SI},a}\\mapsto A_{{\\rm SI},a}+\\partial_a\\chi$ and\n$\\psi\\mapsto e^{iq_{\\rm SI}\\chi/\\hbar}\\psi$. It leaves $F=dA$ invariant and\nmakes $D_a\\psi$ transform by the same phase. This is the covector form of the\nSI potential rule in [[def-em-gauge-transformation]]. Gauge functions in the\nlocal variation argument are compactly supported; no assertion is made about\nlarge gauge transformations, nontrivial bundles, boundary charges, or\nasymptotic sectors.\n\nThe model adopts the separately specified free Dirac representation of\n[[post-qft-free-field-model]] and the positive free photon representation of\n[[post-qft-free-photon-model]] as the free-field correspondence used to\ndescribe the selected species. This extra correspondence does not quantize\nthe interacting classical action. In particular, this postulate supplies no\ninteracting continuum four-dimensional QED Hilbert space, no globally\nwell-posed coupled PDE, no pointwise operator-valued composite current, no\nscattering or LSZ construction, and no regulator-removal or\nnonperturbative-existence result.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "not-applicable"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted full-text Chapter 6",
              "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S6.html",
              "locator": "§6.3.1 for the Dirac current, minimal coupling and local U(1) covariance; §§6.2–6.3 for the free photon and coupled Maxwell–Dirac model."
            },
            {
              "title": "Mark Srednicki, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted 2006 prepublication book draft",
              "url": "https://web.physics.ucsb.edu/~mark/ms-qft-DRAFT.pdf",
              "locator": "§58, printed pp. 345–347, for the spinor-electrodynamics current, local U(1) transformation, and covariant derivative; §§54–55 for the Maxwell action and photon conventions. The source uses Heaviside–Lorentz units and c=ℏ=1, translated to the selected SI/natural map."
            }
          ]
        },
        "library": "physics"
      },
      {
        "id": "pthm-qft-photon-physical-properties",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Two physical photon degrees and positive free dynamics",
        "reference": "research/extended-frameworks-2026-10-03/quantum-field-theory/workers/qed/proofs.md#Q3",
        "design_state": "Proves the positive transverse fiber, auxiliary null quotient and nonnegative free spectrum conditionally on the named current draft suppliers.",
        "dependency_level": 8,
        "deps": [
          "post-qft-free-photon-model",
          "def-qft-photon-transverse-space",
          "def-qft-framework-units",
          "lem-qft-photon-null-quotient",
          "lem-qft-photon-covariance-spectrum",
          "lem-qft-second-quantized-spectrum",
          "def-countable-choice"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "post-qft-free-photon-model": "physical-assumption",
          "def-qft-photon-transverse-space": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-qft-framework-units": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "lem-qft-photon-null-quotient": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-photon-covariance-spectrum": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-second-quantized-spectrum": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "physical_scope": "The selected flat-space source-free photon model only: positive transverse one-photon states, the auxiliary null quotient, Lorentz-covariant free dynamics, and its exact Hamiltonian domain; no interacting gauge model or empirical photon state is asserted.",
        "empirical_premises": [],
        "statement": "Assume Countable Choice [[def-countable-choice]] for the selected Fock-space\nconstruction, with the positive constants and physical energy units of\n[[def-qft-framework-units]]. In the adopted model [[post-qft-free-photon-model]], for\n$\\mathbf k\\ne0$ set $\\mathbf n=\\mathbf k/|\\mathbf k|$ and\n$P_T(\\mathbf k)=I_3-\\mathbf n\\mathbf n^{\\mathsf T}$. Then for almost every\nnonzero momentum, $P_T(\\mathbf k)$ is a positive orthogonal projection of\nrank two, and the positive one-photon Hilbert space is its closed range\n$\\mathcal H_T\\subset L^2(\\mathbb R^3,d^3\\mathbf k;\\mathbb C^3)$. This\ndescription chooses no global continuous polarization frame.\n\nIf an auxiliary four-polarization space\n$\\mathcal K=L^2(\\mathbb R^3,d^3\\mathbf k;\\mathbb C^4)$ with indefinite form\n$[\\epsilon,\\delta]=\\int\\epsilon^\\dagger\\eta\\delta\\,d^3\\mathbf k$ is used,\nthe physical subsidiary space\n$\\mathcal K_0=\\{\\epsilon:-\\epsilon^0+\\mathbf n\\cdot\\boldsymbol\\epsilon=0\n\\text{ a.e.}\\}$ has null radical\n$\\mathcal N=\\{b(\\mathbf k)(1,\\mathbf n):b\\in L^2\\}$. The quotient\n$\\mathcal K_0/\\mathcal N$ is isometric to $\\mathcal H_T$ with positive\ninner product. The physical Fock Hamiltonian\n$H_\\gamma=\\hbar c\\,d\\Gamma(|\\mathbf k|)$ is self-adjoint, nonnegative, and\nhas the exact domain and strongly continuous Lorentz-covariant mass-cone\naction in [[lem-qft-photon-covariance-spectrum]]. The vector-valued\nauxiliary space is not a positive state space, and none of its negative\ndirections is assigned a negative Born probability.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted full-text Chapter 6, §6.2",
              "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S6.html",
              "locator": "§6.2.1 for transverse Coulomb-gauge modes and the two physical polarization components; §6.2.2 for the distinct indefinite auxiliary four-polarization construction and its subsidiary condition."
            },
            {
              "title": "Mark Srednicki, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted 2006 prepublication book draft",
              "url": "https://web.physics.ucsb.edu/~mark/ms-qft-DRAFT.pdf",
              "locator": "§55, printed pp. 335–338, equations (55.3)–(55.25), for the transverse projection, two helicities, canonical commutator, and free photon Hamiltonian. Formal plane-wave expressions are replaced here by the conditional Hilbert-space suppliers."
            }
          ]
        },
        "library": "physics",
        "proof_strategy": "direct"
      },
      {
        "id": "pthm-qft-photon-local-observables",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Local covariant free field-strength and Weyl observables",
        "reference": "research/extended-frameworks-2026-10-03/quantum-field-theory/workers/qed/proofs.md#Q4",
        "design_state": "Proves the conditional local field-strength and bounded Weyl-observable properties with the exact test-function normalization and domains.",
        "dependency_level": 8,
        "deps": [
          "post-qft-free-photon-model",
          "def-qft-framework-units",
          "lem-qft-photon-local-field-strength",
          "lem-qft-photon-smeared-potential",
          "lem-qft-photon-local-weyl-observables",
          "def-countable-choice"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "post-qft-free-photon-model": "physical-assumption",
          "def-qft-framework-units": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "lem-qft-photon-local-field-strength": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-photon-smeared-potential": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-photon-local-weyl-observables": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "physical_scope": "Gauge-invariant observables of the specified positive transverse free-photon Fock model, smeared with compactly supported real tests; local commutativity applies to spacelike-separated supports, while the Coulomb-gauge potential is not claimed local.",
        "empirical_premises": [],
        "statement": "Assume Countable Choice [[def-countable-choice]] for the constructed Fock\nrepresentation. In the adopted model [[post-qft-free-photon-model]], let\n$h^{ab}\\in C_c^\\infty(\\mathbb R^{1,3};\\mathbb R)$ be a real antisymmetric\ntwo-tensor test. By the natural field-strength normalization of\n[[def-qft-framework-units]], choose each component of $h^{ab}$ with unit\n$\\mathrm m^{-2}$. Since $f_{ab}$ has unit $\\mathrm m^{-2}$ and $d^4x$ has\nunit $\\mathrm m^4$, $f(h)$ below is dimensionless. The corresponding\none-particle vector $g_h$ has profile unit $\\mathrm m^{3/2}$ under the\ncoefficient formula of [[lem-qft-photon-smeared-potential]]: its effective\ntest $j^i=-\\partial_a h^{ai}$ has unit $\\mathrm m^{-3}$, the Fourier\nintegral contributes $\\mathrm m^1$, and the factor $(2\\omega)^{-1/2}$\ncontributes $\\mathrm m^{1/2}$. Thus its Hilbert norm under $d^3\\mathbf k$\nof unit $\\mathrm m^{-3}$ is dimensionless, as is the Weyl parameter\n$\\sqrt2\\,g_h$. This is the test normalization adopted here, not a universal\ntest-function unit. Here $f_{ab}$ is the\nnatural-normalized field-strength\ndistribution of the selected free model, corresponding to $F_{ab}$ in the\nmathematical free-photon suppliers and distinct from the SI tensor\n$F_{{\\rm SI},ab}$. Its smearing\n$$f(h)=\\frac12\\int f_{ab}(x)h^{ab}(x)\\,d^4x$$\nis a well-defined operator-valued distribution on the common finite-particle\ndomain $\\mathcal D_{\\rm fin}$, not a pointwise field operator. It is gauge\ninvariant and covariant under the selected free mass-cone unitary action.\nFor two such tests with spacelike-separated supports,\n$[f(h),f(\\ell)]=0$ on $\\mathcal D_{\\rm fin}$. Let $g_h$ be the associated\none-particle test vector and define the Weyl observable\n$W_h:=W_{\\rm Segal}(\\sqrt2\\,g_h)$ as in\n[[lem-qft-photon-local-weyl-observables]]. These are bounded unitaries of\nnorm one; their real and imaginary parts are bounded Hermitian operators\nand commute for spacelike-separated supports. No locality claim is made for\na Coulomb-gauge potential.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted full-text Chapter 6, §§6.2.1–6.2.2",
              "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S6.html",
              "locator": "Coulomb-gauge transverse quantization and the separate Lorenz-gauge auxiliary construction in Chapter 6; these formal mode formulas motivate, but do not replace, the local domain proof."
            },
            {
              "title": "Mark Srednicki, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted 2006 prepublication book draft",
