      {
        "id": "texp-qft-photon-auxiliary-comparison",
        "kind": "thought-experiment",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Auxiliary negative vector versus physical quotient",
        "reference": "research/extended-frameworks-2026-10-03/quantum-field-theory/workers/qed/proofs.md#Q3",
        "design_state": "Gives an explicit normalized negative-norm auxiliary wavepacket and a positive physical transverse comparison.",
        "dependency_level": 9,
        "deps": [
          "pthm-qft-photon-physical-properties",
          "def-qft-framework-units",
          "lem-qft-photon-null-quotient",
          "lem-smooth-bump-between-concentric-euclidean-balls",
          "def-countable-choice"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "pthm-qft-photon-physical-properties": "physical-result",
          "def-qft-framework-units": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "lem-qft-photon-null-quotient": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-smooth-bump-between-concentric-euclidean-balls": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "physical_scope": "A hypothetical exact comparison between an indefinite auxiliary four-polarization vector and normalized states in the positive transverse free-photon model; no measurement, negative probability, or empirical event is asserted.",
        "empirical_premises": [],
        "statement": "Assume Countable Choice [[def-countable-choice]] and the positive transverse\nfree-photon model of [[pthm-qft-photon-physical-properties]]. Let\n$\\mathcal K=L^2(\\mathbb R^3,d^3\\mathbf k;\\mathbb C^4)$ carry the indefinite\nform $[\\epsilon,\\delta]=\\int\\epsilon^\\dagger\n\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)\\delta\\,d^3\\mathbf k$. For nonzero\n$\\mathbf k$, put $\\mathbf n=\\mathbf k/|\\mathbf k|$ and define the subsidiary\nsubspace by\n$\\mathcal K_0=\\{\\epsilon:-\\epsilon^0+\\mathbf n\\cdot\\boldsymbol\\epsilon=0\n\\text{ almost everywhere}\\}$. Fix a wave-number scale $\\kappa>0$ in\n$\\mathrm m^{-1}$ under [[def-qft-framework-units]], and let $\\Omega$ be the\nmomentum ball of radius $\\kappa/4$ centered at $\\kappa(0,0,1)$. By\n[[lem-smooth-bump-between-concentric-euclidean-balls]], translate a smooth\nbump $b$ that equals one on the concentric ball of radius $\\kappa/8$ and\nhas support in $\\Omega$. Set $g=b/\\|b\\|_2$, so\n$g\\in C_c^\\infty(\\Omega)$ and $\\|g\\|_2=1$. The auxiliary timelike wavepacket\n$\\epsilon_{\\rm aux}(\\mathbf k)=g(\\mathbf k)(1,0,0,0)$ has\n$[\\epsilon_{\\rm aux},\\epsilon_{\\rm aux}]=-1$ but is not in $\\mathcal K_0$.\nBy contrast, a normalized transverse wavepacket in\n$\\mathcal H_T$ represents a positive physical one-photon state. Therefore\nthe negative auxiliary norm is not a negative Born probability.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted full-text Chapter 6, §§6.2.1–6.2.2",
              "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S6.html",
              "locator": "Chapter 6 contrasts the two transverse Coulomb-gauge physical modes with a four-component Lorenz-gauge auxiliary space and its subsidiary condition."
            },
            {
              "title": "Mark Srednicki, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted 2006 prepublication book draft",
              "url": "https://web.physics.ucsb.edu/~mark/ms-qft-DRAFT.pdf",
              "locator": "§55, printed pp. 335–338, identifies the two transverse helicity modes; §58, printed pp. 345–347, describes the gauge redundancy of the four-potential."
            }
          ]
        },
        "library": "physics",
        "proof_strategy": "direct"
      },
      {
        "id": "texp-qft-qed-neutral-cell",
        "kind": "thought-experiment",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Hypothetical charged periodic cell violates smooth Gauss",
        "reference": "research/extended-frameworks-2026-10-03/quantum-field-theory/workers/qed/proofs.md#Q2",
        "design_state": "Uses the periodic Gauss constraint to refute a hypothetical nonzero net charge on a boundaryless torus.",
        "dependency_level": 11,
        "deps": [
          "pthm-qft-qed-coulomb-constraints",
          "post-qft-qed-local-coupling",
          "def-qft-framework-units",
          "lem-qft-qed-coulomb-constraint",
          "def-countable-choice"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "pthm-qft-qed-coulomb-constraints": "physical-result",
          "post-qft-qed-local-coupling": "physical-assumption",
          "def-qft-framework-units": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "lem-qft-qed-coulomb-constraint": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "physical_scope": "A hypothetical smooth periodic Gauss-law branch on a flat three-torus with no boundary, puncture, or charge-compensating exterior; nonzero total charge is inconsistent with the stated periodic constraint. No real apparatus or observed charged cell is asserted.",
        "empirical_premises": [],
        "statement": "Assume Countable Choice [[def-countable-choice]] and adopt the local\nclassical Maxwell–Dirac action of [[post-qft-qed-local-coupling]]. Also use\nthe smooth periodic Gauss-constraint conclusion of\n[[pthm-qft-qed-coulomb-constraints]] under its stated hypotheses. On\n$\\mathbb T_L^3$ with side length $L>0$ in metres, choose the electron charge\n$q_{\\rm SI}=-e_{\\rm SI}<0$ and a constant nonzero smooth commuting spinor\n$\\psi(\\mathbf x)=\\psi_0\\in\\mathbb C^4$ in the canonical length normalization\nof [[def-qft-framework-units]]. Its source\n$\\rho_q=q_{\\rm SI}\\psi_0^\\dagger\\psi_0$ is smooth and periodic, with SI\ncharge-density unit $\\mathrm{C\\,m^{-3}}$ under the stated field normalization,\nand its total charge is\n$Q=q_{\\rm SI}\\psi_0^\\dagger\\psi_0L^3\\ne0$. In a hypothetical periodic\nconfiguration with no boundary, puncture, or exterior compensating flux,\nno smooth periodic electric momentum can satisfy the derived Gauss\nconstraint\n$\\operatorname{div}\\boldsymbol\\pi_A+\\rho_q=0$. The neutral case\n$Q=0$ is the separate branch supplied by\n[[pthm-qft-qed-coulomb-constraints]] and\n[[lem-qft-qed-coulomb-constraint]]. The setup is a thought experiment,\nnot a report of a physical measurement. The constant spinor is a\nhypothetical field configuration; no Dirac stationarity or observed\ncharged cell is asserted.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted full-text Chapter 6, §§6.2–6.3",
              "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S6.html",
              "locator": "§6.2 for Gauss' law as a scalar-potential constraint and §6.3 for the charged Dirac source; the local argument here uses periodic rather than spatial-infinity boundary conditions."
            },
            {
              "title": "Mark Srednicki, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted 2006 prepublication book draft",
              "url": "https://web.physics.ucsb.edu/~mark/ms-qft-DRAFT.pdf",
              "locator": "§55, printed pp. 335–338, for the Coulomb constraint and its spatial-infinity solution; the hypothetical periodic-cell conclusion is separately proved under its torus hypotheses."
            }
          ]
